# Equity Valuation and AI-Based Portfolio Analysis

### Project Overview

This project combines traditional financial analysis with Artificial Intelligence (AI) and Machine Learning to explore better investment decision-making approaches.

The project is divided into two main parts.

### Part A: Fundamental Valuation of Square Pharmaceuticals PLC

This part evaluates Square Pharmaceuticals PLC, one of the leading pharmaceutical companies in Bangladesh.

**Key Activities:**
- Analysis of five years of financial statements.
- Calculation of Cost of Equity, Cost of Debt and WACC.
- Free Cash Flow to Firm (FCFF) valuation.
- Free Cash Flow to Equity (FCFE) valuation.
- Dividend Discount Model (DDM).
- DuPont Analysis.

**Key Finding:** FCFF and FCFE estimated the fair share values at Tk 258.57 and Tk 245.80, respectively, compared with the market price of Tk 218.80.

### Part B: AI-Based Stock Price Prediction and Portfolio Optimization

This part uses four Indian pharmaceutical companies:

- Sun Pharmaceutical Industries
- Cipla
- Mankind Pharma
- Torrent Pharmaceuticals

Nine Machine Learning and Deep Learning models were tested to predict future stock prices.

**Key Activities:**
- Historical stock price data collection.
- Data denoising and preprocessing.
- Model training and hyperparameter tuning.
- Walk-forward validation.
- AI-based portfolio construction.
- Markowitz Mean-Variance Portfolio Optimization.
- Comparison of portfolio performance using returns, risk and Sharpe Ratio.

**Key Finding:** The traditional Markowitz portfolio provided more reliable results than the AI-based portfolio in this study.

